# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  MLMVPN for Windows — what never goes in the repository
#
#  Three groups, and the reason each one is here matters:
#    1. secrets and the developer's own infrastructure  (leaking these is the harm)
#    2. build outputs and third-party binaries          (hundreds of MB, rebuildable)
#    3. local scratch                                   (noise)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. secrets, credentials, personal infrastructure ─────────────────────────

# Written fresh every time the Google Script tunnel starts. Contains the Apps
# Script deployment id and its auth key — live credentials for one deployment.
data/gst-config.toml

# A developer's scratch Xray config. Points at whatever worker they were testing,
# with the access UUID in it. Not part of the build (see package.json build.files).
carries_cfg.json

# Signing keys, tokens, environment overrides — none of these belong in git.
# The store channel's Ed25519 key lives in ~/.mlmvpn-dev/, outside the tree, and
# must stay there.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
*credentials*.json

# Local machine state that the app or the tools write next to the source.
t.json
traffic_db.json
xray_test_access.log
xray_test_error.log
*.log
!data/sanction-unsupported.log

# Editor/agent local settings — these record absolute paths from one machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
.agents/
.freebuff/


# ── 2. build outputs and third-party binaries ────────────────────────────────

node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
*.asar
*.asar.disabled

# The engine binaries: xray, sing-box, tor, psiphon, openvpn, aether, lantern,
# geph, wintun and their data files. ~450 MB, none of it ours, and all of it
# fetched or built rather than authored. docs/BUILD.md says where each one comes
# from and how to put the folder together.
core/

# Vendored upstream sources kept locally for rebuilding two of those binaries.
# They are large (gst-src alone carries a Rust target/ directory) and each has
# its own upstream repository. docs/BUILD.md names them.
aether-src/
gst-src/

# The Android app has its own repository: github.com/mlmvpn/mlmvpn_android
android/
android.zip

# Snapshots taken before risky changes. This project uses them instead of
# branches for that purpose; they are whole copies of the tree.
backup/

# Generated code-knowledge graph.
graphify-out/


# Output from running the test suites: a real Psiphon datastore, session notices and
# generated configs. Rebuilt by the tests themselves, and it carries live session data.
tests/**/artifacts/

# Has its own repository: github.com/mlmvpn/cloud-web-panel
cloud-web-panel/

# ── 3. local scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Microsoft/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.tmp
*.swp
*~
.release-notes-*.md
